          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nThe fix is complete. Let me provide a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe issue was that the `v` component of Ethereum ECDSA signatures was being serialized inconsistently when converting to JSON. The `Parity::NonEip155` variant was being serialized as a plain integer (e.g., `27`) instead of a hex-encoded quantity like the rest of the library uses.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**File: `/workspace/crates/primitives/src/signature/sig.rs`**\n\n1. **Serialization (lines 419-435)**: Modified the `serde::Serialize` implementation to use `crate::U64` for all `v` field serialization:\n   - `Parity::Eip155(v)` → already used `U64::from(v)` ✓\n   - `Parity::NonEip155(b)` → changed from `(b as u8 + 27)` to `U64::from(b as u8 + 27)`\n   - `Parity::Parity(true/false)` → changed from string literals `\"0x1\"/\"0x0\"` to `U64::from(1/0)`\n   - Tuple serialization → changed from `self.v.to_u64()` to `U64::from(self.v.to_u64())`\n\n2. **Deserialization (lines 560-568)**: Modified the tuple visitor to deserialize `v` as `U64` instead of `u64`, extracting the value via `as_limbs()[0]`\n\n3. **Tests**: Added comprehensive tests to verify:\n   - Non-EIP155 signatures serialize with hex-encoded `v` (e.g., `\"0x1b\"`)\n   - EIP-155 signatures serialize with hex-encoded `v` (e.g., `\"0x25\"`)\n   - Tuple serialization uses hex encoding\n   - Round-trip JSON serialization/deserialization preserves signature values\n\nAll existing and new tests pass successfully.",
